# System Logs Compliance (always binding)

Every change in this repository must preserve the **zero silent failure** contract.
No error, break, or gap may disappear without a registration path.

## Before editing any feature

1. Read `docs/06-super-admin-and-operations/super-admin-live-logs.md`.
2. Read `docs/01-architecture/module-isolation-rules.md` (`@asol/system-logs-core` section).

## Mandatory capture rules

| Situation | Required action |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Caught failure in business logic | `reportSystemIssue()` or `reportPreAuthFailure()` |
| Pre-auth critical file (`validate:error-logging` list) | `reportPreAuthFailure()` in every catch |
| API route | `runTracedBusinessRoute()` wrapper **or** catch + `mapServiceError()` |
| React render failure | `RouteErrorFallback` or error boundary |
| New global failure surface | wire into `@asol/system-logs-core` capture |

## Forbidden patterns

- Empty `catch {}` blocks (except approved generated bootstrap scripts)
- `.catch(() => undefined)` / `.catch(() => null)` without logging context
- Direct imports of legacy `persistent-system-log-repository` or internal sanitizer paths
- Deep imports of `@asol/system-logs-core/*` (use declared doors only)
- Removing `SystemLogCollector`, `SystemLogErrorBoundary`, or bootstrap registration from root layout

## Package boundaries

- Browser code: `@asol/system-logs-core`
- Server code: `@asol/system-logs-core/server`
- Port wiring only in `src/features/system-logs/system-logs-core-bootstrap*.ts`
- Native crashes: `asol:native-crash` via `NativeCrashPlugin` in `@asol/native-core`

## CI gates (must stay green)

```text
npm run validate:error-logging
npm run test:system-logs-core
npm run architecture:check
```

Any change that breaks these gates is incomplete.

## Docs

When behavior, APIs, capture paths, or operational steps change, update matching files under `docs/` in the same change (English only).
